  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "A fair coin is tossed and a fair spinner numbered 1, 2, 3 and 4 is spun once. (a) List the sample space of the experiment. (b) Find the probability of obtaining a head and an odd number. (c) Find the probability of obtaining a number greater than 2. (d) Find the probability of obtaining a tail or the number 4."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: Write out all eight outcomes once; every probability then comes from counting them."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p087_q15.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p087-q15 from workbook page 87."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Pair every coin outcome with every spinner outcome.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "2 coin results × 4 spinner results"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: (H,1) (H,2) (H,3) (H,4) (T,1) (T,2) (T,3) (T,4) — 8 outcomes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Count the outcomes with a head and an odd number.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "(H,1) and (H,3)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 2/8 = 1/4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Count the outcomes whose number is greater than 2.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "(H,3) (H,4) (T,3) (T,4)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 4/8 = 1/2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 4,
      "instruction": "Count the outcomes that are a tail or show 4, listing each only once.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "(T,1) (T,2) (T,3) (T,4) and (H,4); (T,4) has already been counted"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 5/8"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Pair each of the two coin results with each of the four spinner results to give 8 equally likely outcomes, then count the favourable ones for each part."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "(a) (H,1), (H,2), (H,3), (H,4), (T,1), (T,2), (T,3), (T,4) — 8 outcomes  (b) 1/4  (c) 1/2  (d) 5/8"
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "The coin and the spinner are independent, so all 2 × 4 pairings are equally likely and probability reduces to counting. With 'or', an outcome that satisfies both conditions still belongs to the list only once — counting (T,4) twice would give 6/8 and overstate the probability."
    }
  ],
